From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sliva0 <sliva0mk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Add 2 AVPs from RFC 6942
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

RFC 6942 defines these AVPs in the IETF space, which the dictionary has
no entry for at their codes:

  ERP-RK-Request (618): Grouped, 1 member, section 8.1
  ERP-Realm (619): DiameterIdentity, section 8.2

Each entry's type, enumerated values and grouped members are the
document's, from its clauses and AVP tables, and so are its M and V bits
where the document states them.

Generated by Seanchaí (integrations/wireshark/additions.py).
---
 resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
index 56a8586..49c3a0a 100644
--- a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
+++ b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
@@ -2735,6 +2735,14 @@
 				<gavp name="QoS-Profile-Id"/>
 			</grouped>
 		</avp>
+		<avp name="ERP-RK-Request" code="618" mandatory="mustnot" vendor-bit="mustnot">
+			<grouped>
+				<gavp name="ERP-Realm"/>
+			</grouped>
+		</avp>
+		<avp name="ERP-Realm" code="619" mandatory="mustnot" vendor-bit="mustnot">
+			<type type-name="DiameterIdentity"/>
+		</avp>
 		<avp name="Excess-Treatment" code="577" mandatory="may">
 			<grouped>
 				<gavp name="Treatment-Action"/>
